I think the current logic involves looping through the systemConfiguration repeatedly to look for the desired device and fill Bus in. What do you think about the below logic?

```
// Assuming there's a dynamic mux map <muxMap> visible to DeviceConfig object and here

while (!deviceConfigurations.empty())
{
    std::vector<DeviceConfig> unBuiltDevices = deviceConfigurations;
    for (auto& config : unBuiltDevices)
    {
        if (config.buildDevice()) // Build the device using mux info from <muxMap>
        {
            if (config.isMux())
            {
                config.linkMux(); // Inside linkMux(), append to <muxMap> the info of the successfully linked dynamic mux.
                deviceConfigurations.erase(config);
            }
        }
    }
}

// Loop through the systemConfiguration and map MuxChannel to <muxMap> to retrieve Bus info and replace
```

